  "limitations": [
    "Measurements describe one isolated Apple M4 Pro/macOS runner and one headless Chromium build; they do not establish lower-powered-device, cross-browser or field behavior.",
    "The Node and loaded-page first/subsequent observations are not equivalent to process, HTTP-cache or device cold starts.",
    "Standalone and site-page probes retain one cold and one warm diagnostic sample per fixture or route; their p50/p95 values equal that single observation and are not asserted as timing budgets.",
    "Visible-input timing ends at an observed DOM mutation, not paint. Missing sub-threshold Event Timing entries do not prove a fast interaction; the deliberate calibration only proves the observation path can report a long event.",
    "Trace phase durations can overlap. Zero composite-layer events means no such event was exposed in this trace, not zero compositing cost.",
    "The heap probe is a requested-GC diagnostic from one Chromium process. Empty DOM/listener/resource counters and a responsive positive control do not prove every object is collectible or establish a universal memory budget.",
    "Adverse runtime uses an in-process adapter and does not prove HTTP, socket, proxy, backend cancellation or network capacity.",
    "Bundle rows cover selected production package entry points and retained module graphs; they do not establish parse, execution or interaction latency.",
    "Site paint/LCP/layout observations are raw controlled-run entries, not field Core Web Vitals or universal INP. No reference-model, model-provider, backend-capacity or network-performance benchmark is claimed."
